PUBLIC RESPONSE: {A}

The trp attenuator depends on mutually exclusive RNA stem-loops in the trpL leader transcript. Region 1 normally base-pairs with region 2 (pause structure). When the ribosome does not stall (high tryptophan), it covers region 2, freeing region 3 to pair with region 4 and form the terminator. A mutation that abolishes 1–2 pairing leaves region 2 free to pair with region 3 even when the ribosome is covering region 1; the resulting 2–3 antiterminator sequesters region 3 and thereby blocks formation of the 3–4 terminator. Consequently, transcription continues through the operon under repressing (high-Trp) conditions.

B would eliminate the antiterminator, favoring the terminator. C alters the poly-U tract after the hairpin, not the 3–4 stem itself. D and E would not favor antiterminator formation.}

